Sounds like a former throne room. Since the bugbears in the bones file
will no longer be considered throne room population, they'll usually
be peaceful to a chaotic character.

> If your god is really really mad at you, try a helm of opposite
> alignment if you can find one. Once you do a little slaying, your new
> god will think you're OK.

Perhaps i'm not playing the most recent version, but this seems like
profoundly bad advice to me:
When switching alignment via the helmet, both alignment rating and god
anger will be transferred to the new alignment - e.g. before
switching, you had 
chaotic
transgressed (-16)
Mahannan MacLir is angry with you (1)

after switching, it's
lawful
transgressed (-16)
Lugh is angry with you (1)

In addition, switching alignment will nix your protection.

The only benefit would be that a chaotic donning a helm of opposite
alignment wouldn't need quite such a large sacrifice to pacify his/her
deity. Since such alignment-swapping itself doesn't incur god anger,
it could be worth the protection loss in some cases.

